  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fight against MPox  and shelter assistance to vulnerables returnees victims of conflict in the Rwanguba</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the Mpox spike, this project will support vulnerable returnees and host families in the Rwanguba Health Zone &#xa0;with Mpox Prevention and Hygiene support through the distribution of hygiene kits to 700 Households (approx. 3,500 individuals, assuming HH size of 5), distribution of dignity kits to 370 women and girls of reproductive age, and awareness-raising on Mpox in schools, churches, markets, and health facilities to approximately 35,800 individuals (Outcome 1), and in line with Sphere Minimum Standards for Shelter and Settlement, provide shelter support to 60 vulnerable returnee households (approx. 300 individuals) whose homes were destroyed (Outcome 2). This project targets vulnerable returnees in Rwanguba health zone. The Project will target the most vulnerable returnees&#x2019; households and women and girls of reproductive age whose shelters are destroyed, and nearby public places such as schools, churches, markets, and health facilities for awareness raising.</narrative>
  </description>
